
	OOPS !

	We did not include one of the features documented in the

	manual. The Concurrent CP/M User's Guide mentions that the

	CTRL-ALT-DEL sequence used to re-boot the system will prompt you.

	Well, it won't. Due to some last minute problems we were not

	able to include this feature.



	This feature was intended as an extra safeguard against re-booting

	the system while working with the windows. In particular, there

	is a CTRL-DEL sequence with the windows that allows you to switch

	between full screen and the window. Although there is absolutely

	no possibility of re-booting the system with the CTRL-DEL sequence,

	we were worried about the remote possibility that a finger might slip

	causing the ALT key to be depressed.



	If you really believe that the CTRL-ALT-DEL sequence requires a prompt,

	then please jot down your reasons and send them in on the Reader

	Comment Card, found in the back of the Concurrent CP/M User's Guide.

